<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P>It was interesting to read of Madonna's comparison of George Bush to Saddam Hussein. She stated that they both behaved "in an irresponsible manner".<BR><BR><B>This comment alone would be enough to get our vote! But is Madonna considering a new career in politics? She hasn't given any official indication of wanting to follow this course, but she is certainly keen to "clean-up" her earlier image.</B><BR>Her anti-war views are a refreshing change and it would be nice to see a few more politicians thinking like this. Her straight talking would also break with political traditions and it would be nice to hear a politician who says what they mean.<BR><BR>As for her interest in Kabbalah? She claims she is not following other celebrities interest in this 13th century Jewish mysticism and it's her choice to decide what is right for her. If there really is any magic in Kabbalah, maybe it can help her to become President, if she wants to?<BR><BR>But perhaps she really is just happy "being a wife and mother", although somehow we don't think she is the sort of person who can just fade away into a normal family life. <B>Maybe in a few years time we will see Madonna (or Esther) entering the White House? After all, the last celebrity to become President did a pretty good job!</B></P>
<P><STRONG>source: profindpages.com</STRONG></P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


