<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P class=articleheadtypea align=left><STRONG>Madonna has won her legal to ban ramblers from walking across her £9 million country estate, the Planning Inspectorate announced today.</STRONG></P>
<P class=articleheadtypea align=left>A public inquiry ruled the public has no right of access to 15 of 17 contested pieces of land on the pop singer's 1,200 acre Ashton House, in Dorset.</P>
<P class=articleheadtypea align=left><STRONG>The star and her film director husband, Guy Ritchie, objected after the Countryside Agency</STRONG> mapped the estate under the Countryside Rights of Way Act 2000, pointing out the rights of way.</P>
<P class=articleheadtypea align=left><STRONG>MIRROR.UK</STRONG></P>
</font></div>
