<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td align="left">
<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b>Madonna Urges Her Fans To See Michael Moore's 'Fahrenheit 9/11'</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20"><img src="images/topics/live.gif" border="0" Alt="Live" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><SPAN class=blkPnkHover><STRONG>Michael Moore has got Madonna's vote — she urged fans during her concert Wednesday night at New York's Madison Square Garden to go see his provocative new film, "Fahrenheit 9/11."<BR></STRONG><BR>In what seemed to be a genuine, unscripted moment, the</SPAN> <!-- table with ad and links starts here --><SPAN class=blkPnkHover>singer told the audience — which included the filmmaker himself — that <STRONG>she had just seen the film, and that it had really affected her. Moore had screened the film to a crowd of celebrities and members of the press on Monday at New York's Ziegfeld Theater.<BR></STRONG><BR>"<STRONG>I don't think I've ever cried so hard at a movie in my life</STRONG>," Madonna said during a break in her performance. "And I'm sure I still have a lot to learn from it."<BR><BR><STRONG>Madonna also acknowledged Moore's presence, and thanked him for making the film, which opens in New York on Wednesday and nationwide on June 25</STRONG>.<BR><BR>"Not only is it inspiring and educating, but it's proof that people can make a difference, that we can make a difference," she said. <STRONG>"So, Michael, I know you're out there tonight, and I just wanted to publicly thank you for sticking your neck out, for going against the establishment, for giving us the hope."<BR></STRONG><BR>Madonna had originally tried to create a controversial statement against the war in Iraq herself, via her "American Life" video (see <A href="/news/articles/1469995/02142003/madonna.jhtml">"Madonna Defends Her Violent 'American Life' Video"</A>), which was first edited and then withdrawn because she had feared it could be deemed inappropriate at the time (see <A href="/news/articles/1470876/03312003/madonna.jhtml">"Madonna Yanks Controversial 'American Life' Video"</A>). The idea survives in her live set, when she flashes stark images of war on various screens behind her, and her dancers dress like soldiers during the performance of that song. <STRONG>She also covers John Lennon's peace song "Imagine" during her set</STRONG></SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=blkPnkHover><STRONG>source:MTV.com</STRONG></SPAN></P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


<table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFDFEF" width="100%"><tr><td align="center">

<font class="content">Written by <a href="">gugarko</a> on Thursday, June 17 @  W. Europe Daylight Time  [1 reads].</font><br>
<font class="content"">(<a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=3167">comments?</a> | Score: 0)</font>

</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>
<br><br><br><table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td align="left">
<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b>PIT Experience.</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20"><img src="images/topics/live.gif" border="0" Alt="Live" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><IMG src="/re/PIT/Nolito.jpg" align=left border=0>Our reader and <A href="http://www.madonnavillage.it" target=_blank>community</A> member <STRONG>Herminio</STRONG> (AKA <STRONG>Nolito</STRONG>) won the <STRONG>PIT tickets</STRONG> for him and his partner and had the honour to see the <STRONG>Los Angeles</STRONG> show from a privileged point of view. Due to security reasons, and security was really tight, they were not allowed to take anything with them, not even water. So, cameras, cellphones, bags had to be checked in. <BR><BR><STRONG>Herminio</STRONG> has sent us a brief description of&nbsp;his experience along with the pictures and scans from the <STRONG>PIT</STRONG>. </P>
<P>I flew to <STRONG>L.A.</STRONG> from <STRONG>Chicago</STRONG> early in the morning of <STRONG>May 27th</STRONG>. My partner flew from a convention in <STRONG>Miami</STRONG> to meet me in <STRONG>L.A.</STRONG> Even though I could not get authorization from my supervisor to get the day off from work (as a vacation day), I skipped the day and hopped on a plain to see <STRONG>my IDOL of 20 years</STRONG>. The experience was worth all the repercussions that this action had. <BR><BR>We spent the day in <STRONG>LA</STRONG>, at around 4:30 headed up to the venue (<STRONG>The Forum</STRONG>). We were the first ones to arrive. We checked in with <STRONG>Alison</STRONG> who passed us through security, gave us the tickets, walked us to the "green-room", handed us the wristbands and instructed us on what to do and what not to do. The group of fans was divided into two: <STRONG>Pit right</STRONG> and <STRONG>Pit left</STRONG>. We were on <STRONG>Pit right</STRONG> and we were the first ones to be guided to the stage. <BR><BR>At about 7:45, she walked us to the stage. My heart was beating out of my chest as I realized how close I was going to be from <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> and that the entire thing was not a dream but something real that was happening to me. It was amazing to see how this experience brought a group of 20+ strangers together. Only <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>! <BR><BR></P>
<P align=center><IMG src="/re/PIT/PIT_Wristband.jpg" align=middle border=0></P>
<P><IMG src="/re/PIT/PIT_ticket.jpg" align=right border=0>The show started about forty five minutes later. I remember claming my spot and not moving from there. I was looking straight at the stage when through the shadows I spotted <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>, doing her yoga (upside down) flip. I WENT CRAZY, so did everyone else in the right pit. Then the left pit followed. Then the entire stadium roared! <BR><BR>I could not see the audience, since the pits are located behind two huge screens. As <STRONG>The Beast Within</STRONG> played, these gigantic screens rose from the ground and moved to the left and right of the stage. I was on the pit behind the right screen. As the screen rose, I saw the sea of people roaring for <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>. The energy flowed with such intensity, I thought I would faint. But I know better. If I faint, I would miss the entire show. I was not about to do that. <BR><BR><IMG src="/re/PIT/Concert_Announcement.jpg" align=left border=0>Vogue started and <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> appeared. Everyone went crazy. From the moment she made her appearance until the end of the concert she had us screaming, dancing, singing along and calling her name. <BR><BR>I will not get in any more details, but the highlight of the night for me was when she performed <STRONG>Don't Tell Me</STRONG>. At the end of the song, she does the video choreography. <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> moves to the left pit and dances, and then she moves to the right pit. She stands right in front of me and starts dancing. I am jumping to a height that was probably as tall as the pit, hoping to get her attention. And I succeeded. <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> looks down at me, locks eyes with me, I lock eyes with her. For a moment, I know she knows that I exist. And she smiles at me while dancing and looking at me. The guy behind me is shouting and says to me: "Dude, she is giving you your own private dance!" To which I replied, "I know, isn't it amazing!" She then leans over our pit and high-fives my partner. It was absolutely surreal. <BR><BR><STRONG>- Herminio (AKA Nolito)</STRONG> <BR><BR><STRONG>PS - Any other fan who was there that day, pleas contact me through <A href="http://www.madonnavillage.it" target=_blank>Madonna Village</A>. If anyone has any pictures of the stage and the pit is actually on any of the pictures, please let me know. Thanks!</STRONG> </P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


