<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td align="left">
<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b>Guy Ritchie:Swag hit by thieves</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=6"><img src="images/topics/magazines.gif" border="0" Alt="Magazines" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><DIV class=postcolor><B>17/06/2004 - 17:16:47 <BR><BR>A TV show devised by Guy Ritchie, which sets out to catch thieves red handed, has been the victim of a burglary.</B><BR><BR>Five show Swag traps petty criminals in the act and delivers surprise retribution on the thieves.<BR><BR><B>Madonna’s husband, Snatch director Ritchie, came up with the programme idea after his bicycle was stolen outside a London studio.</B><BR><BR>But thieves have left the show’s producers with red faces after swiping tens of thousands of pounds worth of their camera equipment.<BR><BR>Burglars crept into the London edit suite last night, after producers had been working on the final touches of the second series. <BR><BR>TV bosses are relieved the criminals only took the camera equipment and left behind tapes of the show – the result of months of work.<BR><BR>Series editor Syeda Irtizaali said: “It would have been better if the Swag camera crew had been around and on the case. <BR><BR>“The chances of these thieves escaping with anything would have been substantially reduced if our crack team of super-sleuths had been around.”<BR><BR><B>The first series of the show scared away burglars and surprised car thieves in talking cars.<BR><BR>The second series, which starts on June 29, also features celebrities who play criminals, like former Blue Peter presenter Katy Hill who notches up a massive restaurant bill and tries to leave without paying.</B><BR>source:iol.ie </DIV>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


